# Concept 2 — Zoned Template (fixed regions, slotted widgets)

Philosophy: dashboard isn't a freeform grid but a TEMPLATE with named
zones (header / KPI strip / body / rail). Widgets slot into zones; zone
decides size + allowed widget kinds. Editing = pick zone, pick widget.
Layouts stay coherent without manual x/y fiddling.

```
+======================================================+
| ZONE: header        [welcome | note | goal]          |
|  Good morning, Kalle - Thursday, Jun 12              |
+======================================================+
| ZONE: kpi strip     [metric x 2-6]                   |
| +--------+ +--------+ +--------+ +--------+          |
| | 128    | | $1.2M  | |  7     | |  93%   |          |
| | deals  | | value  | | overdue| | on-time|          |
| +--------+ +--------+ +--------+ +--------+          |
+======================================================+
| ZONE: body (2/3)            || ZONE: rail (1/3)      |
| [list|breakdown|trend|tasks]|| [attention|activity]  |
|                             ||                       |
|  LIST: open deals           ||  ATTENTION            |
|  name        stage   amount ||   o Initech    COLD   |
|  Acme Corp   open    $40k   ||   o Acme Corp  COOLING|
|  Globex      nego    $25k   ||  ------------------   |
|  Hooli       open    $18k   ||  ACTIVITY             |
|  ...                        ||   10:42 anna updated  |
|                             ||   10:31 jens created  |
+======================================================+
```

Model change: DashboardBody gains zones: { header, kpis[], body[],
rail[] } instead of raw x/y; renderer owns geometry + responsiveness.

Best for: fast authoring, consistent look across 237 auto-generated
concept dashboards. Trade-off: less expressive than freeform.
